  "full_response": "# **Incident Response Report: Credential Leak in Public GitHub Repository**\n**Incident ID:** IR-2024-05-15-001\n**Date of Report:** May 15, 2024\n**Prepared by:** [Your Name], Security Incident Response Team (SIRT)\n**Status:** Closed (Resolved)\n\n---\n\n## **1. Executive Summary**\nOn **May 14, 2024, at 14:30 UTC**, the Security Incident Response Team (SIRT) was alerted to a **credential leak** involving sensitive API keys exposed in a **public GitHub repository**. The leaked credentials included:\n- **Payment Processing API Key** (Stripe)\n- **Email Service API Key** (SendGrid)\n- **Cloud Infrastructure API Key** (AWS IAM)\n\nThe repository was **publicly accessible for approximately 48 hours** before detection. Upon discovery, immediate containment actions were taken, including **key revocation, repository takedown, and forensic analysis**. No evidence of malicious exploitation was found, but proactive measures were implemented to prevent future incidents.\n\n**Impact Assessment:**\n- **Risk Level:** High (Potential financial fraud, unauthorized cloud access, and email abuse)\n- **Data Exposed:** API keys (no customer PII or payment data)\n- **Exploitation Status:** No confirmed misuse\n\n---\n\n## **2. Incident Timeline**\n\n| **Time (UTC)**       | **Event** |\n|----------------------|-----------|\n| **May 12, 2024, 10:15** | Developer accidentally commits `.env` file containing API keys to a **public GitHub repository** (Repo: `company-app/config`). |\n| **May 14, 2024, 14:30** | GitHub Secret Scanning alerts SIRT to exposed API keys. |\n| **May 14, 2024, 14:45** | **Containment:** Repository made private; GitHub support contacted for takedown. |\n| **May 14, 2024, 15:00** | **Eradication:** All exposed API keys revoked and rotated. |\n| **May 14, 2024, 16:30** | **Forensic Analysis:** GitHub logs reviewed; no evidence of unauthorized access. |\n",
